{"id":426033645,"author":{"login":"danielmiessler","id":50654,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNjU0","gravatar_id":"","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"node_id":"RE_kwDOPsEkG84ZZMHt","tag_name":"v8.761.0","target_commitish":"main","name":"LifeOS 8.761.0 — The One Loop","draft":false,"immutable":false,"prerelease":false,"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:01:37Z","updated_at":"2026-10-28T14:14:12Z","published_at":"2026-10-27T22:03:18Z","assets":[{"id":683245445,"node_id":"RA_kwDOPsEkG84ouX-F","name":"LifeOS-8.761.0-release.mp4","label":"","uploader":{"login":"danielmiessler","id":50654,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNjU0","gravatar_id":"","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"video/mp4","state":"uploaded","size":49670026,"digest":"sha256:0ff97132b93059e0975ab4ef5eaee3306579780df6522afedde97f38161e7ab8","download_count":20,"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:52:10Z","updated_at":"2026-10-27T23:52:12Z"}],"body":"# 🔁 LifeOS 8.761.0: The One Loop\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/59c04882-92e1-490b-ab07-e84c2f46595f\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **One loop now runs at every level.** Every output climbs toward a written ideal state, and something checks whether it got there.\n\n**6,385 commits** · **426 issues and PRs closed** · **50 skills newly public (97 total)** · **2,050 new capabilities** · **18 hooks deleted**\n\n## ✨ What's new\n\n- 🎯 **Direction first.** Every ISA opens with a one-sentence ideal state you confirm *before* any code gets written.\n- 📏 **Assay checks everything.** Every criterion carries its own eval, and an unrun check reads as *unmeasured*, never as a pass.\n- 🧗 **HillClimb + Errata.** Your complaints get logged in your own words, then turned into experiments until a fix actually holds.\n- 🛠️ **Development skill.** Build, Test, Modify and Checkup, sized to the job: a one-file fix runs inline, a new project fans out.\n- ⏰ **Workflows in the cloud.** Scheduled jobs run whether or not your laptop is open, and \"remind me Friday\" just works.\n- 🚨 **Vigil.** One event log that texts you only when something actually matters.\n- 📊 **New Pulse.** A redesigned dashboard that opens on *Today*, and missing data shows as missing instead of fake green.\n- ⚡ **New statusline.** One process, refreshes every second, starts nothing.\n- 💬 **Text your DA.** The real DA over iMessage, with voice notes transcribed on your Mac and a passphrase-gated phone line.\n- 🔒 **Leaner security.** Claude Code's own permissions, git hooks and a kernel sandbox replace 18 noisy guard hooks. Your `.env` travels age-encrypted.\n- 📦 **One-command install or upgrade.** 7.x upgrades in place, backed up first, and nothing you wrote gets overwritten.\n- 🧠 **Fabric, rewritten.** 51 patterns beat the originals head to head and now replace them, plus new thinking skills: Superior, Unify, Simplify and Pareto.\n\n## 🚀 Upgrade\n\nHand `INSTALL.md` to your AI and say **\"install this\"**. Then run **`lifeos doctor`**.\n\n📖 The full notes, with every change explained: [Releases/v8.761.0/README.md](https://github.com/danielmiessler/LifeOS/blob/v8.761.0/Releases/v8.761.0/README.md)\n\n## 🙏 Thank you\n\nA big share of what got fixed came from your reports: @jlacour-git @bnkath2o @ebrett @jaylarr176 @xmasyx @CarbonRaven @DRAZY @schmetti-dev @mj-deving @GRyndStone @jacobo-ortiz @lgertel @hjbrandt @hjo20 @bytebyrobert @christianjgilman @pybe @Steffen025 @rogdex24 @ramazanpolat @maer @sabo961 @willhern829 @aveneri @cammcd @waveman2020-sudo @tzioup @spec-vova @Albyoung @rathko @dedafrost @0bsolescence @theNetworkChuck\n\n<details>\n<summary>All 426 closed issues and PRs</summary>\n\nCloses: #1580,#1584,#1606,#1614,#1665,#1712,#1721,#1732,#1754,#1755,#1777,#1781,#1787,#1788,#1789,#1790,#1791,#1792,#1793,#1794,#1795,#1796,#1797,#1798,#1799,#1800,#1801,#1802,#1803,#1804,#1805,#1806,#1807,#1808,#1809,#1810,#1811,#1812,#1813,#1814,#1815,#1816,#1817,#1818,#1820,#1821,#1824,#1825,#1827,#1828,#1829,#1830,#1831,#1832,#1833,#1834,#1835,#1837